From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Priyadharshini Gowthaman <pgowtham@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 03 Jun 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM:PROTOCOL: sigma_dut: Add RadSec RADIUS-over-TLS support

RadSec (RADIUS/TLS) support for WFA WPA3 SAE TC 24.x:

  ServerReference   - Resolved to IPv4 for auth_server_addr. When a
                      hostname, stored in ap_radius_server_ref and
                      written as auth_server_hostname for TLS CN/SAN
                      verification. When an IP address, auth_server_
                      hostname is NOT written — no CN/SAN check for
                      direct IP connections (TC 24.3 scenario).
                      Falls back to Primary-DNS IP if DNS fails.
  TrustAnchor       - path to trusted CA certificate (PEM)
  ClientCertificate - path to client full-chain PEM

ap_preset_testparameters parses Primary-DNS (and typo Primay-DNS),
writes it to /etc/resolv.conf and stores it in ap_preset_dns as
fallback auth_server_addr when DNS resolution fails.

ap_write_radsec_conf() writes to hostapd.conf:
  auth_server_addr=<resolved IP>
  auth_server_port=<PORT>
  auth_server_hostname=<hostname only, not written for IP ServerReference>
  auth_server_type=TLS
  auth_server_ca_cert=<TrustAnchor, /tmp prefix if bare filename>
  auth_server_client_cert=<ClientCertificate, /tmp prefix if bare>
  auth_server_private_key=<ClientCertificate>
  auth_server_shared_secret=radsec  (RFC 6614 literal)

Note: WPA2-ENT-256 mapping to AP_WPA2_EAP_SHA256 (AKM 5) is preserved
as-is per WFA test spec — TC 24.x sniffer checks rsn_ie_akm_type=5.

Patch-dependency: 114-UPSTREAM-PROTOCOL-EPPKE-CE2-CE3.patch

Signed-off-by: Priyadharshini Gowthaman <pgowtham@qti.qualcomm.com>
